IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `fraud-nouns`
IMPORT `fraud-dates`
IMPORT `fraud-s15`
IMPORT `fraud-penalty`
IMPORT `fraud-s06-s08`
IMPORT `fraud-s09`

-- Fraud Act 2006: TESTS FOR SECTIONS 6 TO 9.
--
-- Every expected value was decided by reading the section and is written beside the assertion.

§ `Tests for sections 6 to 9`

§§ `Section 8: "article"`

GIVEN ordinary IS A BOOLEAN
      program IS A BOOLEAN
      data IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Article case`
`a thing that is` ordinary program data MEANS `Article case` WITH
    `an article in the ordinary sense of the word` IS ordinary
    `a program held in electronic form` IS program
    `data held in electronic form` IS data

`an ordinary article` MEANS `a thing that is` TRUE FALSE FALSE
`an electronic program` MEANS `a thing that is` FALSE TRUE FALSE
`electronic data` MEANS `a thing that is` FALSE FALSE TRUE
`not an article` MEANS `a thing that is` FALSE FALSE FALSE

-- s 8(1): "article" includes any program or data held in electronic form.
#ASSERT `section 8(1): the thing is an article for the purposes of sections 6 and 7` `an ordinary article`
#ASSERT `section 8(1): the thing is an article for the purposes of sections 6 and 7` `an electronic program`
#ASSERT `section 8(1): the thing is an article for the purposes of sections 6 and 7` `electronic data`
#ASSERT NOT `section 8(1): the thing is an article for the purposes of sections 6 and 7` `not an article`

§§ `Section 6: possession etc. of articles for use in frauds`

GIVEN thing IS AN `Article case`
      possession IS A BOOLEAN
      control IS A BOOLEAN
      forFraud IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Possession case`
`a section 6 case of` thing possession control forFraud MEANS `Possession case` WITH
    `the article` IS thing
    `in his possession` IS possession
    `under his control` IS control
    `for use in the course of or in connection with any fraud` IS forFraud

-- s 6(1): the base case: an ordinary article in his possession, for use in a fraud.
#ASSERT `section 6(1): the elements of the offence are made out` (`a section 6 case of` `an ordinary article` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- "or under his control": control without possession suffices.
#ASSERT `section 6(1): the elements of the offence are made out` (`a section 6 case of` `an ordinary article` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
-- Neither in possession nor under control.
#ASSERT NOT `section 6(1): the elements of the offence are made out` (`a section 6 case of` `an ordinary article` FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- Not for use in the course of or in connection with any fraud.
#ASSERT NOT `section 6(1): the elements of the offence are made out` (`a section 6 case of` `an ordinary article` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- s 8(1): a program or data in electronic form is an article.
#ASSERT `section 6(1): the elements of the offence are made out` (`a section 6 case of` `an electronic program` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `section 6(1): the elements of the offence are made out` (`a section 6 case of` `electronic data` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
-- Not an article at all.
#ASSERT NOT `section 6(1): the elements of the offence are made out` (`a section 6 case of` `not an article` TRUE TRUE TRUE)

§§ `Section 7: making or supplying articles for use in frauds`

GIVEN thing IS AN `Article case`
      dealing IS A `Dealing with an article`
      knowing IS A BOOLEAN
      intending IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Making or supplying case`
`a section 7 case of` thing dealing knowing intending MEANS `Making or supplying case` WITH
    `the article` IS thing
    `what the person does with it` IS dealing
    `knowing that it is designed or adapted for use in the course of or in connection with fraud` IS knowing
    `intending it to be used to commit, or assist in the commission of, fraud` IS intending

-- s 7(1)(a): knowing that it is designed or adapted for use in fraud.
#ASSERT `section 7(1): the elements of the offence are made out` (`a section 7 case of` `an ordinary article` `makes it` TRUE FALSE)
-- s 7(1)(b): intending it to be used to commit, or assist in the commission of, fraud.
#ASSERT `section 7(1): the elements of the offence are made out` (`a section 7 case of` `an ordinary article` `makes it` FALSE TRUE)
-- Both.
#ASSERT `section 7(1): the elements of the offence are made out` (`a section 7 case of` `an ordinary article` `makes it` TRUE TRUE)
-- Neither (a) nor (b).
#ASSERT NOT `section 7(1): the elements of the offence are made out` (`a section 7 case of` `an ordinary article` `makes it` FALSE FALSE)
-- Each of the four things: makes, adapts, supplies, offers to supply.
#ASSERT `section 7(1): the elements of the offence are made out` (`a section 7 case of` `an ordinary article` `adapts it` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `section 7(1): the elements of the offence are made out` (`a section 7 case of` `an ordinary article` `supplies it` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `section 7(1): the elements of the offence are made out` (`a section 7 case of` `an ordinary article` `offers to supply it` TRUE FALSE)
-- Does none of the four things.
#ASSERT NOT `section 7(1): the elements of the offence are made out` (`a section 7 case of` `an ordinary article` `does none of these` TRUE TRUE)
-- s 8(1): electronic data is an article; a thing that is not an article is outside section 7.
#ASSERT `section 7(1): the elements of the offence are made out` (`a section 7 case of` `electronic data` `supplies it` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `section 7(1): the elements of the offence are made out` (`a section 7 case of` `not an article` `supplies it` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `section 7(1): makes, adapts, supplies or offers to supply` `makes it`
#ASSERT NOT `section 7(1): makes, adapts, supplies or offers to supply` `does none of these`

§§ `Section 9: participating in fraudulent business carried on by sole trader etc.`

GIVEN knowingly IS A BOOLEAN
      company IS A BOOLEAN
      asIfCompany IS A BOOLEAN
      exempted IS A BOOLEAN
      creditors IS A BOOLEAN
      otherPurpose IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Fraudulent business case`
`a section 9 case of` knowingly company asIfCompany exempted creditors otherPurpose MEANS `Fraudulent business case` WITH
    `knowingly a party to the carrying on of the business` IS knowingly
    `the business is carried on by a company (as defined in section 1(1) of the Companies Act 2006)` IS company
    `the business is carried on by a person to whom section 993 applies as if the person were a company` IS asIfCompany
    `the business is carried on by a person exempted from the application of section 993` IS exempted
    `the business is carried on with intent to defraud creditors of any person` IS creditors
    `the business is carried on for any other fraudulent purpose (as in section 993)` IS otherPurpose

-- s 9(1), (2): knowingly a party; carried on by a person outside the reach of s 993; with intent to defraud creditors.
#ASSERT `section 9(1): the elements of the offence are made out` (`a section 9 case of` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- s 9(2)(b): "or for any other fraudulent purpose".
#ASSERT `section 9(1): the elements of the offence are made out` (`a section 9 case of` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `section 9(1): the elements of the offence are made out` (`a section 9 case of` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
-- Neither purpose.
#ASSERT NOT `section 9(1): the elements of the offence are made out` (`a section 9 case of` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- s 9(1): not knowingly a party.
#ASSERT NOT `section 9(1): the elements of the offence are made out` (`a section 9 case of` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
-- s 9(3)(a): carried on by a company -> within the reach of s 993, so s 9 does not apply.
#ASSERT NOT `section 9(1): the elements of the offence are made out` (`a section 9 case of` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
-- s 9(3)(b): a person to whom s 993 applies as if a company.
#ASSERT NOT `section 9(1): the elements of the offence are made out` (`a section 9 case of` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
-- s 9(3)(c): a person exempted from s 993.
#ASSERT NOT `section 9(1): the elements of the offence are made out` (`a section 9 case of` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- s 9(3) directly.
#ASSERT `section 9(3): the business is carried on by a person within the reach of section 993` (`a section 9 case of` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `section 9(3): the business is carried on by a person within the reach of section 993` (`a section 9 case of` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `section 9(3): the business is carried on by a person within the reach of section 993` (`a section 9 case of` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `section 9(3): the business is carried on by a person within the reach of section 993` (`a section 9 case of` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
-- s 9(2): the business is one to which the section applies.
#ASSERT `section 9(2): the business is one to which section 9 applies` (`a section 9 case of` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `section 9(2): the business is one to which section 9 applies` (`a section 9 case of` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
